  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ヤナギタデ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A4%E3%83%8A%E3%82%AE%E3%82%BF%E3%83%87",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108735913,
      "text": "ヤナギタデ は、タデ科イヌタデ属の一年草。水辺などに生える雑草。和名は、葉がヤナギに似ていることから。マタデ（真蓼）、ホンタデ（本蓼）、カワタデ、ナガボヤナギタデともいう。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Persicaria hydropiper」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persicaria_hydropiper",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1373674118,
      "text": "Persicaria hydropiper, also known as water pepper, marshpepper knotweed, arse smart or tade, is a plant of the family Polygonaceae. A widespread species, Persicaria hydropiper is found in Australia, New Zealand, temperate Asia, Europe and North America. The plant grows in damp places and shallow water. Cultivated varieties are eaten in East Asia for their pungent flavor."
    }
  },
